g, Have mercy on me, O Lord, thou Son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxBut he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWBut he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast it to dogs.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters' table.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›Then Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus' feet; and he healed them:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse"¦verses“„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙáThen Jesus called his disciples unto him, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd Jesus saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book'§chapter«first_verse#ªlast_verse&¦verses”„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ9And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake them, and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlAnd they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets full.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book'§chapter«first_verse'ªlast_verse'¦verses‘„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.¦layout ªlast_verse'